  "contracts": [
    "Positive unique known checkin IDs; caller supplies resolved branch_of_rid and mtime_of_rid defaults. Branch bytes reject NUL, times must be finite.",
    "Input parent rows preserve relative per-node SQL query order; forward rows precede backward rows. Native schema indexes order children by cid and parents by pid in captured query_rows. No canonical ordering is invented.",
    "Shortest uses pending duplicate nodes and pop-time seen, does not turn backwards after a forward edge, and allows first-hop non-excluded cherrypicks only in direction2.",
    "Branch cost0 counts nodes including start at cost1. Positive branch cost starts at0, adds absolute Julian-day distance plus branch-change penalty.",
    "Hidden nodes remain traversable and cost-bearing; initial node never marked hidden. Midpoint and depth use visible steps excluding start.",
    "Common ancestor uses two sides, first shared parent discovered by native queue order, newest matching arena record and predecessor rewiring. Orientation follows native diagnostics, not caller order.",
    "New owned equal-endpoint ancestor returns one node; raw native diagnostic is empty because native does not initialize global path for this early return.",
    "Budget errors distinguish no-path from resource exhaustion; graph constructor does not assert that rows are artifact-validated, authorized, or acyclic. Native seen rules terminate cyclic rows within budgets.",
    "All graph/search-owned dynamic storage uses checked Vec reservations retaining TryReserveError as Error::Allocation and Error::source. The RID lookup is a sorted (rid,index) vector with in-place unstable sort and logarithmic binary search; only this lookup index is sorted. Native adjacency order and heap tie comparisons remain unchanged.",
    "Finite work includes O(V log V + E log V + B) graph indexing/metadata validation, O(V) per-search membership initialization, O(log V) endpoint/hidden lookup, O(S log S + R + S) search/heap/path work with at most V checkins, E input links, B branch bytes, S search records and R row visits. Weighted branch byte comparisons add at most O(S * B) work. Bounds constrain these dimensions; row_visits is not advertised as a total CPU-instruction budget."
  ],
